From 72973ab0f4385c17ff7f08319eee26a222852e15 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kshot3000 <kshot9000@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 16:34:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] docs(operators): update stale Pearl node pin to upstream
 v1.4.8 release

The operator guide pinned the node/presync3 presync branch at commit
d5e5de77 (2026-05-23), which is now ~74 commits behind upstream master and
superseded by official releases (v1.4.8, 2026-09-16). The guide's own
guidance already said to prefer newer upstream releases; this applies it.

The indexer requires pearld >= v1.1.0 on mainnet for the MoE hard-fork
canonical-checkpoint advisory (config.js / persistent-indexer.js), and
v1.4.8 satisfies that.
---
 docs/operators.md | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/operators.md b/docs/operators.md
index daff5c0..8e3dbc5 100644
--- a/docs/operators.md
+++ b/docs/operators.md
@@ -19,8 +19,13 @@ P2P: 44108
 RPC: 44107
 ```
 
-The current operator-tested Pearl node path is the Pearl source branch
-`node/presync3` at commit `d5e5de77c3d48951ddb0d0c25a861d7627b9cab4`.
+The current operator-tested Pearl node path is the official upstream release
+`v1.4.8` (commit `5b09d844e4069440933722c51495ac24a7bb4886`, published
+2026-09-16) from https://github.com/pearl-research-labs/pearl. It includes the
+MoE hard fork — this indexer requires `pearld >= v1.1.0` on mainnet for the
+canonical-checkpoint advisory — and supersedes the earlier `node/presync3`
+presync-branch pin (`d5e5de77`, 2026-05-23), which is now ~74 commits behind
+upstream `master`.
 If upstream Pearl publishes a newer operator release, prefer that release and
 record the exact commit you run.
 
-- 
2.43.0

